{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01QkHn8tU3MFTfZSNbyYTWXP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (one folder, plain-text markdown as source of truth, no database/syncing).\n\n- **Core purpose â€” a personal task/project manager.** It tracks tasks and projects across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) as markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`), with a full task lifecycle: active â†’ done / cancelled / saved-for-later / restored.\n\n- **What it ships as runtime.** `anchor_gui.py` â€” a stdlib-only Python HTTP server that renders an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777` and writes changes straight back to the markdown. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. `anchor.py` mirrors the same logic as a CLI and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Reliability scaffolding.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs daily at 5 AM via Task Scheduler â€” it parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway test server, exercises all endpoints and task-state transitions (with all model calls stubbed), and walks the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces, writing dated reports to `health_reports/`.\n\n- **The major feature layer â€” an \"R&D control surface\" built across four versions** (v2 â†’ v4 \"Project Cockpit\"). It turns each project into a mission-control window for \"trio\"-driven work: a Research â†’ Planning â†’ Build pipeline (skills researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman). Each lane shows its most-recent session as a status-lit tile (green/amber/red/grey) that expands inline into a panel pairing a cached, grounded summary with a real, resizable terminal.\n\n- **Terminal substrate.** v4 standardizes on real **ConPTY** terminals (xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket / SSE transport), each session isolated in its own git worktree+branch. The lane's skill auto-loads **once** and greets once (fixing the v2 repeating-prompt bug). `pywinpty` is the project's single, explicitly-declared native dependency (optional extra, lazy import) â€” everything else is stdlib-only, enforced by `distro.py`'s import scan.\n\n- **Supporting capabilities.** Engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini, Gemini research-only), per-session validated/cached summaries (generate-twice + grounding filter), per-project cost/tokens/time rollups, a \"Grass Catchers\" idea board with promote-to-lane, type-aware deliverable launch (skill/tool verify Â· service preview on a port guaranteed â‰  8777 Â· program run Â· doc render), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n\n**Status (per the docs):** v4 \"Project Cockpit\" was built by Foreman (9 waves GREEN, 637 tests passed) and merged to master on 2026-06-13.\n\nOne caveat on grounding: these claims come from the project's own `CLAUDE.md` and frozen design docs, not from independently re-reading the source. If you want, I can verify any specific claim against the actual code."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b89c9520-e8b3-427d-bf12-1c4ac8904bba","uuid":"20e2253f-442f-479c-bf1f-9c4c831ff89b","request_id":"req_011Cc1fMmJhrK52MMHhn95gK"}
